This file exists so that `backend/data/` does.

Everything the directory normally holds is ignored: the 359 MB build
database, the raw DLD release, the audit log. Without a committed file
the directory is absent from a fresh checkout, and the image build fails
at `COPY backend/data/ ./data/` with `"/backend/data": not found` --
which is exactly how CI went red while every local build stayed green.

`.dockerignore` re-includes this one file for the same reason. Market
data is optional at boot by design (D-074); the directory is not.
